    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27653" root="ظلم" body-key="Z">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظِلَامٌ</span></b> : see 1, near the beginning: ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  see also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظِلَّامٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  It signifies also <i>Little,</i> or <i>small, in
quantity:</i> or <i>mean, contemptible, paltry,</i> or <i>of no
weight</i> or <i>worth:</i> ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  whence the saying, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَظَرَ إِلَىَّ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظِلَامًا</span>, meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَزْرًا</span> [i. e. <i>He looked at me from
the outer angle of the eye, with anger,</i> or <i>aversion</i>]. (K.)

